            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नस (nas) is a tadbhava: CDIAL lists Hindi nas, \"muscle, tendon, vein, nerve\", under Sanskrit snasā, \"sinew\" (CDIAL 13784). Everyday Hindi uses one word for every cord under the skin."
